# Git commit author

When creating commits in this repository, always set the author and committer email to `francesco.pan@gmail.com`.

Do **not** run `git config` to change this. Pass env vars on each commit:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME='Francesco Pandolfi' \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL='francesco.pan@gmail.com' \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME='Francesco Pandolfi' \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL='francesco.pan@gmail.com' \
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Message here.
EOF
)"
```

Note: `git push` uses GitHub credentials, not the commit email. The email above affects commit metadata only.
